                <tr>
                  <th style="border: 1px solid #777; padding: 5px 12px; background: #eef5ee;">Formula Type</th>
                  <th style="border: 1px solid #777; padding: 5px 12px; background: #eef5ee;">Build It</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="border: 1px solid #777; padding: 5px 12px;">Recursive</td>
                  <td style="border: 1px solid #777; padding: 5px 12px;">a<sub>n</sub> = a<sub>n - 1</sub> + <span style="color: #087a2e; font-weight: bold;">-7</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="border: 1px solid #777; padding: 5px 12px;">Explicit</td>
                  <td style="border: 1px solid #777; padding: 5px 12px;">a<sub>n</sub> = <span style="color: #087a2e; font-weight: bold;">-7</span><span style="color: #1f77b4; font-weight: bold;">n</span> + 19</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <br><br>
            <div style="margin: 2px 0;">A negative card after a plus sign means subtract: a<sub>n - 1</sub> + -7 is the same as a<sub>n - 1</sub> - 7.</div>
          </div>
        </td>
        <td style="width: 42%; vertical-align: top; padding: 0 0 0 8px;"><br><br>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 8px; padding: 9px; margin: 0 0 8px 0; background: #f8fbff;">
            <div style="font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">What to Look For</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">Find the repeated change first.</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">The recursive formula needs <strong>a<sub>n - 1</sub></strong>, not a<sub>1</sub>.</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">The coefficient of <span style="color: #1f77b4; font-weight: bold;">n</span> is the <span style="color: #087a2e; font-weight: bold;">common difference</span>.</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">The constant is not always the first term.</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">Test the explicit formula using n = 1.</div>
          </div>
          <br>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 8px; padding: 9px; margin: 0 0 8px 0; background: #fffaf2;">
            <div style="font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">Shortcut</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">For arithmetic sequences:</div>
            <div style="margin: 5px 0; padding: 6px 8px; border: 1px solid #ddd; background: #fff;">
              <div style="margin: 2px 0;">Recursive: a<sub>n</sub> = a<sub>n - 1</sub> + d</div>
              <div style="margin: 2px 0;">Explicit: a<sub>n</sub> = dn + b</div>
            </div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">The same <span style="color: #087a2e; font-weight: bold;">d</span> goes in both formulas.</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">Find <strong>b</strong> by making the formula work for n = 1.</div>
          </div>
          <br>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 8px; padding: 9px; margin: 0 0 8px 0; background: #fff;">
            <div style="font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">Shortcut Example</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">Sequence: <span style="color: #8a5a00; font-weight: bold;">8, 13, 18, 23, ...</span></div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">Change: <span style="color: #087a2e; font-weight: bold;">+5</span></div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">Recursive: a<sub>n</sub> = a<sub>n - 1</sub> + 5</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">Explicit starts as a<sub>n</sub> = 5n + b.</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">Use n = 1: 5(1) + b = 8, so b = 3.</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0; color: #087a2e; font-weight: bold;">a<sub>n</sub> = 5n + 3</div>
          </div>
          <br>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #b98b8b; border-radius: 8px; padding: 9px; margin: 0 0 8px 0; background: #fff7f7;">
            <div style="font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">5. Common Mistakes</div>
            <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse;">
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td style="width: 45%; vertical-align: top; padding: 4px; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; font-weight: bold;">Mistake</td>
                  <td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 4px; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; font-weight: bold;">Fix</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 4px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">Using a<sub>1</sub> in the recursive formula</td>
                  <td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 4px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">Use a<sub>n - 1</sub>, the previous term.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 4px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">Using the first term as the coefficient</td>
                  <td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 4px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">The coefficient of n is the common difference.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 4px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">Using the first term as the constant</td>
                  <td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 4px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">Test n = 1 to find the constant.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 4px;">Losing the negative sign</td>
                  <td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 4px;">If the sequence decreases, the common difference is negative.</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <br>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 8px; padding: 9px; margin: 0; background: #f4fff5;">
            <div style="font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">6. Final Check</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">Does the recursive formula use a<sub>n - 1</sub>?</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">Does the recursive change match the repeated change?</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">Does the coefficient of n match the repeated change?</div>
            <div style="margin: 3px 0;">When n = 1, does the explicit formula give a<sub>1</sub>?</div>
            <div style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; color: #087a2e; font-weight: bold;">If all four checks work, your formulas probably match the sequence.</div>
          </div>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
